// Package subject's DEPTH fixtures, generated as linear nesting chains.
//
// THEY ARE SIZED BY MEASURED FRAME DEPTH, NEVER BY A LEVEL COUNT COPIED FROM
// ANOTHER IMPLEMENTATION. The frames-per-nesting-level ratio is a property of
// the walk's recursion structure, so a chain that comfortably exceeds one walk's
// ceiling can sit far below another's. Both chains bottom out in a chan so the
// under-control proves it still REPORTS through its whole depth rather than
// merely surviving it.
package subject

// UnderCeiling is the deep-but-LEGITIMATE control: 64 nesting levels, about a
// quarter of the ceiling in frames. The quarter is deliberate. A structural
// change that increases frames-per-level pushes an over-fixture further into
// true refusal, which is harmless, but pushes a control like this one OVER the
// ceiling, where it would red against correct code. Only this side needs margin.
type UnderCeiling0 struct{ Next UnderCeiling1 }
